WEBVTT

NOTE Music: "The Escalation" by Kevin MacLeod (incompetech.com), CC BY 3.0.

1
00:00:00.704 --> 00:00:04.835
NoticerMap. Every feature, with Mark Carney as the example.

2
00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:11.282
Start with the Tours button: guided walks through the map, node by node, with sources.

3
00:00:11.736 --> 00:00:17.723
The Tours page lists every guided walk, each with its number of steps and a Start tour button.

4
00:00:21.196 --> 00:00:27.766
The notice opens on a first visit, and the About this map link at the bottom of the sidebar reopens it.

5
00:00:27.766 --> 00:00:36.250
It says what the map is: compiled with the help of AI research assistants from public sources, with every entry linked to its source.

6
00:00:37.707 --> 00:00:51.332
And what it is not: items marked reported are not independently verified, leads are not evidence of wrongdoing, and nothing alleges that anyone broke the law unless a court or official body has found so.

7
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.172
Click I understand to accept the notice.

8
00:00:57.128 --> 00:01:01.750
Back at the top, the How to use button, under the logo, starts the walkthrough.

9
00:01:03.208 --> 00:01:06.296
It has thirteen steps. Step one is Search:

10
00:01:06.296 --> 00:01:10.561
type a name, group, bill or record number, or press slash.

11
00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:15.896
Next. Step two, Search filters, explains each filter.

12
00:01:15.896 --> 00:01:19.331
Step three, Source layers, explains the layers.

13
00:01:19.331 --> 00:01:22.255
Skip closes the walkthrough at any time.

14
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:32.553
Along the top: Map, Tours, Networks, Follow the money, Timeline, Leads, Overlaps, Index, Sources, About.

15
00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:37.144
Search and filters on the left. Interactive map in the middle.

16
00:01:37.144 --> 00:01:38.612
Profiles on the right.

17
00:01:39.069 --> 00:01:47.958
Search everything: networks, lobby groups, NGOs, names, places, dates, aliases, bills and records. Press slash. Type Carney.

18
00:01:48.414 --> 00:01:52.823
Results show their source layers. For example, open Mark Carney.

19
00:01:54.051 --> 00:01:58.737
Here Carney is the centre node. Lines are the claims linked to Carney.

20
00:01:59.202 --> 00:02:02.201
Click any node for its profile. Mark Carney:

21
00:02:02.201 --> 00:02:09.290
Prime Minister of Canada, and former Governor of the Bank of Canada and Governor of the Bank of England.

22
00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:13.516
Badges name the source layers. Here there are 105 connections:

23
00:02:13.516 --> 00:02:18.629
39 verified in public records, 1 partly verified, 65 reported by an outlet.

24
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.948
Scroll for sources, money and every claim.

25
00:02:21.948 --> 00:02:25.962
A reported badge means only that the source outlet said it.

26
00:02:25.962 --> 00:02:27.936
There are five labels in all.

27
00:02:28.393 --> 00:02:31.653
Layouts: Network, Rings, Province, Clusters.

28
00:02:31.653 --> 00:02:37.730
Names toggles labels. Line colour switches between status, relationship and layer.

29
00:02:51.395 --> 00:02:58.428
Hide hubs thins crowded nodes. Scroll to zoom, drag to pan, double-click a node to expand it.

30
00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:10.482
Now the filters. The walkthrough has a Search filters step that explains each one, with a More filters section.

31
00:03:17.542 --> 00:03:23.849
Topics first. Click Carney: 113 entities and 197 claims.

32
00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:28.928
Filters stack. Across groups, an item must pass every one.

33
00:03:28.928 --> 00:03:31.932
Inside a group, any chip left on is enough.

34
00:03:32.387 --> 00:03:37.372
Claim status: click Verified. 71 entities, 79 claims.

35
00:03:38.788 --> 00:03:41.713
Add Type: Person. 5 entities, 3 claims.

36
00:03:41.713 --> 00:03:44.114
Every filter narrows the result.

37
00:03:44.646 --> 00:03:48.927
To widen, click another chip. Organization joins back in.

38
00:03:49.381 --> 00:03:53.696
Province keeps jurisdictions. Relationship groups claims:

39
00:03:53.696 --> 00:03:59.678
money, influence, role and more. Lobbying limits lobbied and lobbied-on claims.

40
00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:09.257
Also: date range, money only, legal status, and Outside the norm, a comparison to a sourced benchmark, not a finding of wrongdoing.

41
00:04:09.257 --> 00:04:12.392
Seen in at least asks for two or more layers.

42
00:04:12.847 --> 00:04:15.962
Search finds matches without narrowing the map.

43
00:04:15.962 --> 00:04:19.410
Hits your filters hide are marked hidden by filters.

44
00:04:19.867 --> 00:04:22.441
Reset filters clears everything at once.

45
00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:35.109
Source layers choose whose reporting you see, including Immigration, and People and boards.

46
00:04:35.109 --> 00:04:39.034
Turn off Public records: 57 entities, 112 claims.

47
00:04:41.274 --> 00:04:44.077
Theories are separate, and off by default.

48
00:04:44.077 --> 00:04:48.349
Tick Theories, under People, to include them, marked unverified.

49
00:04:48.806 --> 00:04:55.007
The Theories layer holds claims and connections from sources not yet backed by public records.

50
00:04:56.062 --> 00:05:02.113
Tick it. A notice says: unverified, reported claims only, no wrongdoing alleged.

51
00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:07.330
For Carney, 14 theory items join the map:

52
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:13.723
113 entities become 127. Claims and money totals do not change.

53
00:05:14.835 --> 00:05:21.676
His profile lists the theories that name him, each marked unverified, with a records check beside it.

54
00:05:22.732 --> 00:05:29.914
Why it matters: you can see what is claimed, check it against the records, and spot leads to investigate.

55
00:05:29.914 --> 00:05:33.882
Over time, a theory can be tested, confirmed or ruled out.

56
00:05:34.938 --> 00:05:38.408
Untick it, and the map returns to the documented links.

57
00:05:43.098 --> 00:05:53.048
Networks lists 33 curated groupings, such as board interlocks and shared funders, each with its own sources and status badge.

58
00:05:53.048 --> 00:05:57.427
The 679 auto-detected clusters are hints, not findings.

59
00:05:59.887 --> 00:06:02.437
Follow the money. The Carney selection:

60
00:06:02.437 --> 00:06:05.576
two recorded flows, twenty-one thousand dollars.

61
00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.768
Choose Mark Carney, tick only through selected:

62
00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:16.049
one flow, 1,750 dollars, a donation from Bruce Flatt, labelled partly verified.

63
00:06:16.049 --> 00:06:19.230
Estimates stay out unless you tick them.

64
00:06:19.689 --> 00:06:28.087
Timeline: 182 dated claims, in lanes by relationship or status, by event date or first reported.

65
00:06:33.763 --> 00:06:36.833
Leads are timing patterns in public data:

66
00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:40.427
a question to check, not evidence of wrongdoing.

67
00:06:40.427 --> 00:06:42.524
Timing alone shows no cause.

68
00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:48.411
For Carney: Davos, and a Brookfield pact review at Davos, two days apart.

69
00:06:48.411 --> 00:06:50.866
Leads are not fully verified yet.

70
00:06:51.324 --> 00:06:56.793
Overlaps are links the map found: shared funders, people, places, sources.

71
00:06:56.793 --> 00:07:01.301
84 match the Carney selection. Never counted in money totals.

72
00:07:01.762 --> 00:07:04.640
Index lists matching entities, sortable.

73
00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:10.181
Sources, listed with search. About explains the badges, method and downloads.

74
00:07:22.628 --> 00:07:27.756
How are these connected shows up to three shortest chains of sourced links.

75
00:07:27.756 --> 00:07:35.826
Carney to Freeland: this shows one chain runs through the Government of Canada, both links verified in public records.

76
00:07:41.421 --> 00:07:51.462
Note windows, top right. Drag a node into the note window to paste the information from a search result or profile title, or use Copy to note.

77
00:07:54.413 --> 00:08:00.784
Notes stay in this browser only. You can Export as markdown, text or JSON files.

78
00:08:02.389 --> 00:08:08.142
Every entity has its own page: each connection, with date, amount, source and status.

79
00:08:14.603 --> 00:08:20.198
If you see a mistake or have a suggestion, report a correction on any claim:

80
00:08:20.198 --> 00:08:22.553
email, or a public GitHub issue.

81
00:08:48.731 --> 00:08:52.969
If you get a little lost, the How to use button will replay the walkthrough.

82
00:08:56.032 --> 00:09:03.663
Enjoy this investigative open source tool to help people expose the truth that is being kept from we the people.

83
00:09:03.663 --> 00:09:10.681
May we the people all enjoy health, happiness and prosperity against the odds of these darkening times.

